.TH NCDU\-CLEAN 1 "October 2026" "ncdu-clean 0.2.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ncdu\-clean \- delete files found with ncdu, keeping a journal and a quarantine
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ncdu\-clean browse
.RI [ options ]
.I EXPORT
.br
.B ncdu\-clean suggest
.RI [ options ]
.I EXPORT
.br
.B ncdu\-clean rm
.RI [ options ]
.RI [ PATH ...]
.br
.B ncdu\-clean log
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B ncdu\-clean restore
.RI [ options ]
.RI [ RUN
.RI [ PATH ...]]
.br
.B ncdu\-clean list
.RI [ options ]
.I EXPORT
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ncdu\-clean
works on an export made by
.BR ncdu (1)
(\fBncdu \-e \-o scan.json /path\fR).
It lets you browse the export, mark files and directories, and then choose what
to do with them: delete them, move them to a quarantine, or save the list.
The journal entry is written before the file is removed. Quarantined files
can be put back where they came from.
.PP
With an export, each path is checked against that export before removal.
A file whose size or modification time changed since the scan, or a directory
that gained files, is refused.
.B rm
without \fB\-\-export\fR skips this check and warns.
Paths at the top of the tree (\fB/\fR, \fB/etc\fR, \fB/var\fR, ...), the home
directory and the root of the scan are always refused.
Every action is simulated first; nothing is done without \fB\-\-yes\fR or an
explicit confirmation in the browser.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B browse \fIEXPORT\fR
Browse the export like
.BR ncdu (1).
Mark items with Space, then press
.B x
to simulate the selection and choose: delete permanently, quarantine, or save
the list to a file.
Options:
.RS
.TP
.BI \-o " FILE" ", \-\-out " FILE
Keep the selection in
.I FILE
as you go, and reload it if it exists.
.TP
.BI \-\-log " FILE"
Journal to use.
.RE
.TP
.B suggest \fIEXPORT\fR
Ask
.B $NCDU_CLEAN_AI
for a plan. The command reads a JSON summary of the export on standard
input and writes a JSON object on standard output:
.IP
{"items": [{"path": "/var/tmp/old.log", "action": "delete", "reason": "old log"}]}
.IP
.B action
is
.B delete
or
.BR quarantine .
On a large export, the forty largest entries are sent (the first level,
then the biggest names inside those).
Paths that are not in the export are dropped. A top-level path
(\fB/\fR, \fB/etc\fR, \fB/var\fR, ...), the home directory and the root of
the scan are dropped. A directory is dropped when something inside it has
the other action.
A user profile directory, \fBpagefile.sys\fR, \fBswapfile.sys\fR, \fBhiberfil.sys\fR,
and the Windows, System32, SysWOW64 and WinSxS directories are dropped from
a suggestion. They can still be marked by hand in the browser. The result is printed as JSON when standard output is not a terminal.
The summary also lists mounted disks (size and free space), removable disks,
and disks that are present but not mounted.
The model may name one quarantine folder on a writable mount
(\fBquarantine_to\fR).
A folder that is not on a known writable disk, or that overlaps a path in the
plan, is replaced by the writable disk with the most free space.
A removable disk is used first. A folder on the scan disk is not kept while
a removable disk is mounted.
On a terminal, reading the export and waiting for the model are separate
screens: each shows the phase, a running clock, the disks, and the key you just
pressed.
q cancels the wait.
With \fBNCDU_CLEAN_AI_THINK=1\fR the model thinks first.
The screen shows that duration, then the plan as the JSON arrives.
The thinking text is kept in the suggestion log.
The plan then shows the paths and the quarantine folder.
The bottom line shows the arrows, F1 and q.
F1 lists the keys.
t moves the selected line from Delete to Quarantine, or the other way.
\- takes the selected line out of the plan.
d deletes the lines under Delete, m moves the lines under Quarantine into
the folder (the folder is created when it does not exist).
q or Esc quits and returns the terminal at once.
Enter returns to the file list.
d and m ask for confirmation.
If the model fails, that screen says why. Nothing
is removed,
and the journal is not written, until that confirmation.
Options:
.RS
.TP
.BI \-\-delete\-list " FILE"
Write the paths to delete, one per line, for
.BR "rm \-\-from" .
.TP
.BI \-\-quarantine\-list " FILE"
Write the paths to quarantine, one per line.
.RE
.TP
.B rm \fIPATH\fR...
Check, then delete or quarantine the given paths (for scripts).
Simulation by default.
Options:
.RS
.TP
.BR \-y ", " \-\-yes
Really act.
.TP
.BI \-e " EXPORT" ", \-\-export " EXPORT
Check that nothing changed since the scan.
Without this option, that check is skipped.
.TP
.BR \-r ", " \-\-recursive
Allow non-empty directories.
.TP
.BI \-\-trash " DIR"
Move into
.IR DIR / RUN /...
instead of deleting.
.TP
.BI \-\-from " FILE"
Read paths from
.IR FILE ,
one per line (\fB\-\fR means standard input).
.TP
.BR \-0 ", " \-\-null
Paths are separated by NUL.
.TP
.BI \-\-log " FILE"
Journal to use.
.RE
.TP
.B log
Show the journal: date, action, size, path.
Options:
.BI \-\-grep " TEXT"
filters on the path,
.BI \-\-last " N"
keeps the last N lines.
.TP
.B restore \fR[\fIRUN\fR [\fIPATH\fR...]]
Without argument, list the quarantine runs with their state.
With a run identifier (or a prefix, or
.BR last ),
put its files back where they came from; with paths, put back only those.
Nothing is ever overwritten: if the destination exists, the file stays in the
quarantine and a conflict is reported; existing directories are merged.
Simulation by default; use
.B \-\-yes
to act.
Directories re-created on the way get default permissions.
.TP
.B list \fIEXPORT\fR
Flat list of the files of an export, biggest first, as
.IR size <TAB> path .
Options:
.BR \-\-dirs ,
.BI \-\-min\-size " SIZE" ,
.BI \-\-top " N" ,
.BR \-\-apparent ,
.BR \-0 .
.SH BROWSER KEYS
.TP
.BR Up / Down ", " j / k
Move.
.TP
.BR Right / Enter ", " l
Open the directory.
.TP
.BR Left / Backspace ", " h
Parent directory.
.TP
.B Space
Mark or unmark the item (a whole directory if it is one).
.B [*]
is marked, and
.B [+]
is covered by a marked directory above.
.TP
.B p
Ask for a suggestion and mark it. Nothing is removed. A plan with both
actions is marked in two passes.
.TP
.B x
Act on the selection.
.TP
.B c
Clear the selection.
.TP
.BR s ", " n
Sort by size, by name.
.TP
.B a
Switch between disk usage (space really taken, what you get back) and file
size (length of the content).
.TP
.BR ? ", " q
Help, quit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/ncdu\-clean/deleted.jsonl
Default journal (\fI/var/log/ncdu\-clean.jsonl\fR for root), one JSON object per
line and per file.
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/ncdu\-clean/quarantine/
Default quarantine.
Moving files there does not free disk space.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B NCDU_CLEAN_LOG
Journal to use when
.B \-\-log
is not given.
.TP
.B NCDU_CLEAN_AI
Command run by
.B suggest
and by the
.B p
key. It reads the JSON summary on standard input and writes the JSON plan
on standard output.
.I examples/suggest-openai.py
in the source tree is such a command for an OpenAI-compatible endpoint.
It reads
.BR NCDU_CLEAN_AI_URL ,
.B NCDU_CLEAN_AI_MODEL
and, when the endpoint requires one,
.BR NCDU_CLEAN_AI_KEY .
The key is sent only to that endpoint. It is not written to the journal.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
ncdu \-e \-o scan.json /var
ncdu\-clean browse scan.json
NCDU_CLEAN_AI="python3 examples/suggest-openai.py" \\
NCDU_CLEAN_AI_URL="http://127.0.0.1:11434/v1/chat/completions" \\
NCDU_CLEAN_AI_MODEL="qwen2.5" \\
ncdu\-clean suggest scan.json \-\-delete\-list delete.list \-\-quarantine\-list quarantine.list
ncdu\-clean rm \-r \-e scan.json \-\-from delete.list
ncdu\-clean rm \-r \-e scan.json \-\-from quarantine.list \-\-trash ~/q
ncdu\-clean rm \-r \-e scan.json /var/tmp/old \-\-trash ~/q \-\-yes
ncdu\-clean restore
ncdu\-clean restore last /var/tmp/old/file.log \-\-yes
.fi
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success; 1 if some path was refused, missing, in conflict or failed; 2 on
usage or input errors.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ncdu (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Thomas Lloancy
